  "verbalization": "Eteplirsen is associated with Muscular Dystrophy through a chain of indications that link it to Golodirsen, which in turn is linked to Muscular Dystrophy. This suggests a potential role for Eteplirsen in the treatment of muscular dystrophy, possibly through a mechanism similar to that of Golodirsen. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Eteplirsen may be repurposed for conditions such as Becker and Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy, both of which are forms of muscular dystrophy. The shared indication of Muscular Dystrophy across these paths implies a possible overlap in therapeutic mechanisms, though the exact relationship remains unclear. The presence of Ataluren in one path adds another layer of complexity, suggesting that Eteplirsen might interact with other therapies targeting similar pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Eteplirsen could be a viable candidate for repurposing in muscular dystrophy, though further research is needed to clarify its specific mechanism of action.",
